                <pb facs="0249" n="167" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg167"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.51/747.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the American Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-07-12"><hi rendition="#italic">July 12,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Instructs him to renew, if necessary, his demands for the punishment and
                    dismissal of the Dominican official and for the future protection of the
                    American customs officials. Further instructs him to point out to the Dominican
                    Government its obligation under the treaty to afford full protection.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
